  "figure_caption": "EXPLORATORY post-hoc time resolution of the pre-registered carry-phase probe result \u2014 no new claim, same rows/targets/discipline at finer time grain. Selectivity = real pooled held-out R\u00b2 minus mean shuffled R\u00b2 (5 group-coherent shuffles, each with its own alpha search); band = \u00b11 shuffled std. GroupKFold(5) by SEED, shuffles group-coherent by EPISODE; identical rows and folds for all four lines. Bins 1.6 s (32 steps @20 Hz), span \u22126.4..+9.6 s, retained only if \u2265120 rows and \u226515 episodes (8 retained; dropped: [-6.4,-4.8)s (n=64 < 120 rows); [+8.0,+9.6)s (n=75 < 120 rows)). Median lift-off +0.70 s. Headline unchanged: peak carry-phase selectivity 0.227 (R\u00b2 0.189) at DiT L28, below the 0.3 bar.",
  "figure_note_on_png": "EXPLORATORY post-hoc re-cut of the pre-registered carry-phase probe result \u2014 no new claim; full method caption in timecurve_summary.json.",
  "peak_vs_pre_registered_headline": "The DiT L28 line peaks at selectivity 0.356 (R\u00b2 0.341, shuffled std 0.013) in the [+3.2,+4.8) s bin (centre +4.0 s) on n=181 rows, ABOVE the pre-registered phase-bucket value of 0.227 (R\u00b2 0.189, carry mask, n=809). Read it as a NOISIER single-bin estimate, NOT a better result: those 181 rows are 8% of the 2,413 captured rows and about 22% the size of the pre-registered 809-row carry cell, and the bin was selected as this line's maximum over 8 bins (a max-over-bins statistic is upward-biased). The study's headline is unchanged and stays below the 0.3 certificate bar.",
  "precontact_reading": "Pre-contact bins (3 retained, \u22124.8..0.0 s): the largest selectivity is +0.044 (physics ceiling (wrist F/T, k=16 window), [-3.2,-1.6) s), but the largest REAL pooled held-out R\u00b2 over all four lines and all pre-contact bins is only +0.0039 \u2014 i.e. no line predicts mass better than the training-fold mean before contact. Those small positive selectivities come from the shuffled control scoring NEGATIVE (shuffled R\u00b2 \u2248 \u22120.02..\u22120.05, the usual grouped-CV behaviour when a permuted per-episode label is fit across folds), not from real pre-contact signal. Nothing here qualifies the study's leakage story: the pre-registered guard (mass selectivity < 0.1 at every probed cell on the precontact mask) also still holds at this grain.",
